{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/944540-a-few-questions","id":944540,"title":"A few questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-05T14:58:11-07:00","id":944540,"title":"A few questions","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I would like to clear something for myself, if possible. Also, if these questions were answered somewhere else, please direct me to those answers. So, without further ado:<br /> 1. Why do the Disciple level direct damaging spells deal only bashing damage? I mean, all the weapons in the game are dealing Lethal damage, so where is the logic that, for example, wind blades (Matter - Windstrike) deal bashing damage?<br /> 2. When casting an area effect spell with a duration, does the duration affect the area or the people or things in it? For example, if I cast AoE Enhance Skill with 24 hours duration, does the duration affect only an area and everyone who remains in it, or does it affect the people gathered in that area?<br /> 3. If the spell is affecting an area is it possible to specify whom would it affect? Something like a Key in Space Arcana? For example, previous AoE Enhance Skill affects an area and anyone who enters it and says a short phrase would gain the benefit as long as they are in the area.<br /> 4. For Keys, would it be possible to specify something more unusual? For example, spell affects anyone who is enraged. What practice would it require?<br /> <br /> Of course, I have a my own ideas about solving these things, but I would like to hear other opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12217-bjelokrili","name":"bjelokrili","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T15:53:53-07:00","id":944579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bjelokrili</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/944540-a-few-questions#post944540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello!<br /> <br /> I would like to clear something for myself, if possible. Also, if these questions were answered somewhere else, please direct me to those answers. So, without further ado:<br /> 1. Why do the Disciple level direct damaging spells deal only bashing damage? I mean, all the weapons in the game are dealing Lethal damage, so where is the logic that, for example, wind blades (Matter - Windstrike) deal bashing damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems most like a conscious decision of the authors' parts. Apparently directly damaging someone is just difficult for magic to do. Mages tend to disable opponents in different ways, so that the game gets more creative than just damaging spells over and over if combat does break out. There are ways to instantly disable someone in the first three dots of any arcanum, so I would not worry about being weak because you can &quot;only&quot; deal bashing damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. When casting an area effect spell with a duration, does the duration affect the area or the people or things in it? For example, if I cast AoE Enhance Skill with 24 hours duration, does the duration affect only an area and everyone who remains in it, or does it affect the people gathered in that area? </div> </div> </div>It's pretty vaguely written, I will grant you that. It is not made very clear what the Subject is when casting an Area spell, but obviously the Area cannot be the Subject itself, as that would make most area spells pointless. I think the easiest way to see it is this: an Area spell makes everyone/everything (as appropriate) within it a Subject of the spell. So it would buff the people in that area, and they are then free to leave the area and maintain the buff, but new people entering the area later are not buffed. I could be wrong, though, this stuff is confusing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. If the spell is affecting an area is it possible to specify whom would it affect? Something like a Key in Space Arcana? For example, previous AoE Enhance Skill affects an area and anyone who enters it and says a short phrase would gain the benefit as long as they are in the area. </div> </div> </div>Look up Warding gesture, p. 136.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. For Keys, would it be possible to specify something more unusual? For example, spell affects anyone who is enraged. What practice would it require? </div> </div> </div>Why not? I don't think it needs a second arcanum at all, Space keys seem fully capable of this on their own. But if not, it would probably be Add Mind, to peer into emotions. Don't think it is needed though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T16:13:57-07:00","id":944586,"title":"","content":"Because Mage deciding to deal you damage isn't stopped by anything. You can't dodge it, no Attribute will help you, Mage picks any number between 3 and ~8 and they just inflict it on you. Mage damage is so efficient that party of one of posters here one-round bombed a God with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-05T22:21:10-07:00","id":944709,"title":"","content":"Can't you use Reach to boost damage to Lethal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T00:17:43-07:00","id":944745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/944540-a-few-questions?p=944709#post944709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't you use Reach to boost damage to Lethal?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, you need to have 4 dots of an arcana to deal direct lethal damage and then from there you can deal aggravated with a reach and a mana. You can however deal lethal with indirect effects, like a forces 2 or 3 spell to make an existing source of fire jump onto somebody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T01:47:46-07:00","id":944757,"title":"","content":"So was my answer concerning how Area spells work correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T05:08:04-07:00","id":944787,"title":"","content":"Dave said 2 or 3 pages ago in a Ask a Simple Question that Area Spells simply affect all viable subjects inside the area. So instead of choosing to raise corpse you touch (no scale factors), or 5 chosen corpses (advanced scale: subjects), you raise all corpses in a small room (advanced scale: area) that then can leave the area normally. So basically, it's correct.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> If you want to make an Area a Subject, you simply need a way to perceive &quot;Area&quot;. This seems like a job for either Space Sight, or a Space Knowing Spell. Mage 2 subject system is pretty good - you can target pretty much anything, from people to thoughts, but you need a way to properly perceive them first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 08-06-2016, 09:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:19:24-07:00","id":944997,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1292_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1292\" data-vbnamecard=\"1292\">Unahim</a>: Thank you for the answers! And, believe me, I am well aware of how powerful the mages are. I didn't ask that question because I think mages are weak in terms of harm they can do (and my personal opinion is that whoever thinks that shouldn't really play Mage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), but because of the logic of things. As I said in example, Windstrike specifically attacks a target with a heavy curtain of wind or water. That seems like a weapon to me. And nothing prevents a Mage to shape the curtain as blades...<br /> Also, Warding Gesture seems like a good choice, but I am unsure how would I put it into practice. Consider the next scenario: You have a fortress under siege and you want every defender of the fortress to have their skill enhanced while on the fortress ground (AoE Enhance Skill with Area as a target, I guess), while at the same time denying the same effect to attackers. How would you use Warding Gesture in that case. I thought it could be solved with specifying something like a Key from Space Arcana. After all, if it can be done in Space Arcana, isn't it logical it can be done in other Arcanums?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1292_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1292\" data-vbnamecard=\"1292\">Unahim</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a>: Thank you for the clarification of the Area effects. I was hoping it was something like that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> And why isn't mage direct damage stopped by anything? Shouldn't by definition each Arcanum be able to stop the damage from itself (Practice of Shielding)? Even grant armor (or Withstand effect) against it's effects? I mean Prime can do that against all Arcana, and Vampire with resilience can stop quite a bit of damage from Mage direct damaging spells...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12217-bjelokrili","name":"bjelokrili","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T12:50:27-07:00","id":945010,"title":"","content":"A curtain of air and water is not as damaging as anything solid could be, unless you are considering incredibly high pressures or speeds. The &quot;shape&quot; of the water has no effect, since it will reshape itself as soon as it smacks the target. Sure, enough speed can still break your bones or as cut you open... but you need so much pressure that I imagine it being equivalent to doing so much bashing damage that it rolls over into lethal territory, which is already there in the system. Contrast that with how CoD uses lethal, to imply that even a small dagger or a brick are lethal, even if not swung with too much force.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T13:30:48-07:00","id":945033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bjelokrili</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/944540-a-few-questions?p=944997#post944997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> And why isn't mage direct damage stopped by anything? Shouldn't by definition each Arcanum be able to stop the damage from itself (Practice of Shielding)? Even grant armor (or Withstand effect) against it's effects? I mean Prime can do that against all Arcana, and Vampire with resilience can stop quite a bit of damage from Mage direct damaging spells...</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out the Counterspell attainment on page 192. It lets you use your Gnosis + Dots in Arcanum to defend against any spell of that Arcanum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T13:38:53-07:00","id":945035,"title":"","content":"Sure, if you will prepare in advance to defend against that specific damaging spell, it will work. Problem is that once Mages hit 3 dots in in an Arcanum, they can creative thaumaturge up infinite variations of their damaging spell using all of the different things falling under it's purview - Death might tear you up with shadow tentacles, assault you with cold of grave, or make your meat rot. <br /> This is why I'm personally happy with Shadow Name merit being so powerful - Mages will cling to their Shadow Named patterns, thus if you know you are going to end up fighting Burner McBurn, you can expect him to try burning you at least once, so it's a good idea to get Resist Fire. <br /> <br /> As for Keys...remember that Keys are special feature of Space Arcanum. Think carefully before allowing to replicate them using different Arcana. <br /> <br /> As for &quot;shaping stuff as blades and things&quot; - you are welcome to create a spell that does that, but it will probably require an Attack roll (something like Gnosis+Athletics/Firearms) and won't give you benefits of normal damaging spell - it won't be sure-fire. It's a good trade off, I think. They also often require more actions than one and won't act immediately; &quot;transforming water into blades&quot; would be one spell, and then throwing it at your opponents would be another, taking two actions at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:09:51-07:00","id":945121,"title":"","content":"Counterspell doesn't work against a specific spell does it? I was under the impression you just needed to counter the arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:17:11-07:00","id":945126,"title":"","content":"You need to have your action for the turn left unspent, observe the act of spellcasting under appropiate Mage Sight, and then use up your action in response to being cast at to contest the casting.<br /> The big problem about this is that you give up your action that could do something productive to <i>attempt a chance</i> at cancelling other's party move. Situation has following resolutions:<br /> a) You win, dude doesn't complete his spell.<br /> b) You lose, dude completes his spell.<br /> Either way, you give up your action. If there is no one else to stop the guy, he can just try again next turn. Counterspell is a very situational power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T16:50:18-07:00","id":945151,"title":"","content":"Well, a damaging spell isn't so sure fire if it has to be thrown, which very well may cause paradox as well. But in general, yeah, mages don't need to be more powerful when it comes to killing things. Combat is a thing because fantasy, but Mage is about solving Mysteries. There's a reason mages don't go around picking fights with whatever is in their way at the moment: wisdom is important to hold on to for survival. You go around killing things on a regular basis and you'll start losing a lot of wisdom. And if you inure yourself to wisdom loss for your attack spell, then you'll be knee deep in paradox. And possibly having your spell countered.<br /> <br /> As to choosing who you affect, I think there's a fate ruling spell that does that...<br /> <br /> With keys, I typically restrict that to the Space arcanum, but the keys themselves can be whatever you want them to be. A particular state of mind, some rare concoction, a particular time of day, or even a password. The sky is the limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T02:18:57-07:00","id":945370,"title":"","content":"You don't have to guard against specific spell. For example, Mind Shield in Mind Arcanum protects against all Mind spells (including direct damage) by initializing Class of Wills (as written in Errata). So why cannot other Arcana have similar Shielding effect? Forces Shield, Matter Shield and so on.<br /> <br /> And, if there is already a spell that gives you Withstand rating against all spells (Wards and Signs, p168), why can't there be a spell in each Arcana that gives you Withstand rating against all spells from that Arcanum?<br /> <br /> And I am aware of the counterspell mechanics. And I agree with WHW about it. It is great in situations where you have advantage of numbers, but in One on One is quite situational...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12217-bjelokrili","name":"bjelokrili","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T02:38:37-07:00","id":945377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bjelokrili</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/944540-a-few-questions?p=945370#post945370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to guard against specific spell. For example, Mind Shield in Mind Arcanum protects against all Mind spells (including direct damage) by initializing Class of Wills (as written in Errata). So why cannot other Arcana have similar Shielding effect? Forces Shield, Matter Shield and so on.<br /> <br /> And, if there is already a spell that gives you Withstand rating against all spells (Wards and Signs, p168), why can't there be a spell in each Arcana that gives you Withstand rating against all spells from that Arcanum?<br /> <br /> And I am aware of the counterspell mechanics. And I agree with WHW about it. It is great in situations where you have advantage of numbers, but in One on One is quite situational...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Ghost Shield in Death has been errata'd to work against any Death spell too, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}